   "text": "This is an artemisinin-type structure: the dihydroartemisinin core with a thiomorpholine 1,1-dioxide ring on the acetal-adjacent carbon in place of the usual OH or OR group.\n\n**Ring system**\n- A cyclohexane ring carries a hashed methyl on one carbon and the ring-fusion CH, which has a hashed H.\n- A tetrahydropyran ring contains the CH(CH3) carbon (wedged methyl), the CH bearing the nitrogen substituent (hashed bond), the ring oxygen, and the acetal carbon (wedged H).\n- The 1,2,4-trioxane bridge runs from the quaternary carbon (hashed bond to the peroxide O) through the O\u2013O bond to the carbon bearing a hashed methyl. That carbon is also bonded to the acetal carbon through the second bridging oxygen.\n- A CH2CH2 bridge links the second ring-fusion CH (hashed H) to the methyl-bearing bridgehead carbon.\n\n**Substituent**\n- The nitrogen belongs to a six-membered ring N\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013S(=O)(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013CH2, which is thiomorpholine 1,1-dioxide.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each centre by hand from its wedge or hash bond and the neighbour order in the SMILES. This was not checked with software, so an individual @/@@ could be wrong.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H]1CC[C@H]2[C@@H](C)[C@H](N3CCS(=O)(=O)CC3)O[C@@H]4O[C@@]5(C)CC[C@@H]1[C@]42OO5"
